						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#838">Guild Rules</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							The Enigmatic Council states some rules to abide by:<br />
<br />
Please note that there will always be exceptions to every rule. The Enigmatic Council reserves the right to rule on any issues in a manner they feel to be &quot;fair.&quot;<br />
<br />
<br />
1) For now little experience is required to join our banner ((minimum of 12 seasons)).<br />
<br />
2) If you wish to have a friend/companion join with us:<br />
<br />
<br />
A) YOU must vouch for their worthiness and are thus held responsible for this new addition to the Banner once they have been accepted. We highly recommend that this be somebody you trust and/or is somebody that you enjoy adventuring with.<br />
<br />
B) To be accepted, at least one of the Enigmatic Council must approve the candidate. This approval process is left up to the council member, but this member of the council must not also be the one that suggested the member. (e.g. It takes two baby.)<br />
<br />
<br />
3) ((We are a moderate role-playing guild, and as such have made a ruling on names such as &quot;Imgunnaget Ewe&quot;--or something similarly anti-RP--inappropriate and thus not allowed.))<br />
<br />
4) Being one of us is a matter of pride and you should always wear the crest of Enigmatic Souls with your head held high ((Please try and leave /anon off. It is much appreciated if we would all either use /role-play or keep both toggled off so that your guild tag is showing at all times)).<br />
<br />
5) Everything that you do reflects on the guild as a whole and as such, should cause you to conduct yourselves well and with excellent manners at all times. ((This encompasses many different issues including--but not limited to--KSing, Ninja-looting, heh and power looting for that matter as well. Please feel free to post any additions you feel are needed here to the guild message board.))
						</td>
					</tr>
